{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkuffU3HEXHJWdXAnN4CiZ","type":"tool_result","content":"814\t**rows.cljc, deleted.**\n815\t- `check-label-bytes!` (`:212-230`): the label-size bound; nothing grows\n816\t  any more.\n817\t- Inside `canonical-numbering` (`:236-355`): the label seeding\n818\t  (`:252-255`), `ce-slot`/`ce` (`:257-284`), `positions` (`:285-325`),\n819\t  `classes` (`:326-330`), `refine` (`:331-337`), `search` (`:338-354`),\n820\t  and the `checked-encode`/`checked-key`/`checked-sort` wrappers\n821\t  (`:245-251`). The `[:child (checked-encode id)]` spelling (`:273-275`)\n822\t  goes with `ce`.\n823\t- `default-budget` (`:200-202`): the `:label-bytes` key; the `:search`\n824\t  key too in the D5 variant (with D6 it stays and counts trials).\n825\t\n826\t**rows.cljc, rewritten.**\n827\t- `canonical-numbering` (`:236-355`), same signature and contract\n828\t  (`task`, optional `budget` → `{source-id :yin.k/cc-n}`; empty census →\n829\t  `{}`), now the root run of §2: `descriptors` extended by the two\n830\t  synthetic kinds `:entry` and `:component`; body ranks from the census;\n831\t  `enter`/`unordered`/`fixpoint`/`components`/`component-encoding`/\n832\t  `adopt`/`resolve`/`local-run`/`spell` as in the prototype\n833\t  (`collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj`, sections \"runs\" and\n834\t  \"spelling\"), with `spend!` charged as §2 \"Work\" says; the totality\n835\t  assertion before returning; D5 raising `:yin.k/non-portable\n836\t  :unresolved-cursor-cells` (D5 variant) or D6 charging `:search`.\n837\t  Portable `.cljc` per continuation §12: no `@#'` reflection, `mapv`/\n838\t  `into`/`reduce` (not `for`) over sequences that may exceed 32 elements\n839\t  (the prototype's `components` uses `for`; replace), `contains?` for\n840\t  membership, `(assoc {} …)` never `(assoc nil …)`, atoms are fine on all\n841\t  three hosts.\n842\t- `emit-node` (`:181-197`): thread a row path so a child's D5 refusal\n843\t  reports `[12 <install name> …]` (D5 variant only; otherwise unchanged).\n844\t- `decode*` recompute (`:570-575`): wrap the `emit` call (which numbers\n845\t  the root and every child) so that only `:yin.k/non-portable\n846\t  :unresolved-cursor-cells` becomes `:yin.k/undecodable\n847\t  :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the path prefixed by `root`; a\n848\t  `:resource-limit` propagates (D5 variant only; with D6 the recompute\n849\t  is unchanged apart from the budget keys).\n850\t- Namespace docstring (`:1-17`): \"canonical cursor-cell numbering\" →\n851\t  \"discovery-order cursor-cell numbering (design note §2)\".\n852\t\n853\t**rows.cljc, kept unchanged.** `row-table`, `pending-table`, `node`,\n854\t`refuse!`/`bad!`, the marker checks, `bytes-key`/`compare-bytes`/\n855\t`byte-compare`/`sorted-bytes`, `descriptors`, the census order\n856\t(`:137-156`), `emit-slot`/`emit-node` apart from the path, `spend!`\n857\t(`:205-209`), `emit-numbered` (`:358-363`), `emit` (`:366-372`),\n858\t`structural?`, `literal?`, `check-abstract!`, all of `decode*` before\n859\t`:570` and after `:575` (the order numbering → `validate-frames`,\n860\t`:576-578`, stays), `decode`, `canonical-under`, `frame->rows`,\n861\t`rows->frame`, `validate-frames`, and the `:bytes`, `:rows`, `:depth`,\n862\t`:cursor-cells`, `:work` budget keys with their defaults.\n863\t\n864\t**rows_test.cljc, kept as fixtures and tests.** `task-node`,\n865\t`cursor-cell-body`, `fixture` (`:16-37`), `portable-frame` and the\n866\t`bijection` test, `row-ids-are-jing-default`, `replace-row`,\n867\t`window-sorted-and-unique`, `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`\n868\t(`:143-156`), `alias-topology-and-census` (`:159-168`),\n869\t`gates-and-graph-before-hashes`, `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`\n870\t(`:206-213`), `schema-and-literal-canonicality`,\n871\t`child-scope-and-shared-child-dag` (`:240-249`),\n872\t`pending-envelope-and-nil-literal-are-preserved`,\n873\t`task-root-checks-carried-code-and-frame`, `reversed` and\n874\t`unordered-containers-are-order-free` (`:285-304`),\n875\t`census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` (`:331-338`), the marker tests\n876\t(`:341-381`), `cursor-cell-and-identity-shaped-literal-are-distinct`\n877\t(`:384-389`), and the fixture `seven-cursor-cell-triangle-square`\n878\t(`:392-397`). Every counterexample of §6 becomes a fixture (items 12–16\n879\tbelow), including the refused ones.\n880\t\n881\t**rows_test.cljc, rewritten.**\n882\t- `refinement-search-on-symmetric-cursor-cells-is-bounded` (`:171-178`)\n883\t  → `symmetric-cursor-cells-number-by-the-component-rule`: same two\n884\t  assertions on equal roots and two numbers; the `{:search 1}`\n885\t  assertions become `{:work 1}` → `:yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit`.\n886\t- `canonical-roots-are-pinned` (`:307-328`): `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n887\t  stay; the loop plus 2-cycle block loses the `{:search 2}` assertion and\n888\t  the pin `55ff168e…`; under D6 it pins `858a891e…` with `L = cc-1`\n889\t  (and the renamed task equal); under the D5 variant it asserts the\n890\t  `:unresolved-cursor-cells` refusal with path `[15]` and cells `[A B]`.\n891\t- `intermediate-label-bytes-are-bounded` (`:400-403`) →\n892\t  `seven-cursor-cells-number-by-residue-search` (D6: root `d76d787a…`,\n893\t  11 trials, `{:search 10}` → `:resource-limit [:search]`) or, in the D5\n894\t  variant, `seven-cursor-cells-are-refused` (`:unresolved-cursor-cells`,\n895\t  cells `[a b c d e f g]`).\n896\t- `input-row-bodies-do-not-spend-label-bytes` (`:406-421`) →\n897\t  `large-literals-do-not-spend-work-beyond-their-bytes`, same body: a\n898\t  400000-element literal still emits and decodes under the default\n899\t  budget.\n900\t\n901\t## 9. Acceptance for the rewritten 6a numbering\n902\t\n903\t12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y`,\n904\t    the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`, the\n905\t    witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]` and the two frame fixtures of §6,\n906\t    `canonical-numbering` returns exactly the maps of §6.\n907\t13. `rows-test/review-counterexample-resolves-by-fixpoint`: `'a #{X Y}`,\n908\t    `'b X` numbers `X cc-1, Y cc-2`; the task renamed and with the set\n909\t    reversed gives the same root; the root is pinned `a3713a5e…`.\n910\t14. `rows-test/component-rule`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`, `{X 1, Y 1}`,\n911\t    `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` and `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]` number without refusal;\n912\t    element reversal and renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`,\n913\t    `da69c679…`, `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`, `92747c0f…`.\n914\t15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n915\t    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n916\t    pinned `65ba4530…` and `409548a7…`; `#{[#{X Y} #{X Y}] [#{P Q} #{R S}]}`\n917\t    numbers and is pinned `b35b8e12…`; the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`\n918\t    numbers `A cc-1, B cc-2`, is pinned `9600fe01…` and decodes.\n919\t16. D6: `rows-test/residue-search`: the 2-cycle, the 3-cycle, the path,\n920\t    the loop plus 2-cycle and the seven-cell state number with the pins\n921\t    of §6 (`0fe898cc…`, `0b181cd4…`, `726a9fbb…`, `858a891e…`,\n922\t    `d76d787a…`), renaming plus shuffling gives equal roots, every\n923\t    carrier decodes, and the 3-cycle under `{:search 1}` refuses\n924\t    `:yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit [:search]`.\n925\t    D5 variant instead: `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the\n926\t    same five states refuse at `emit` with `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind\n927\t    `:unresolved-cursor-cells`, path `[15]` and the component's sorted\n928\t    cursor cells; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered` decodes to\n929\t    `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the path prefixed\n930\t    by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a parent whose\n931\t    install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with path\n932\t    `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n933\t    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n934\t17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n935\t    unchanged; `a3713a5e…`, `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`, `7dc3d5c4…`,\n936\t    `6ea03f9b…`, `9600fe01…` added; `55ff168e…` removed.\n937\t18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (one to six\n938\t    cursor cells over two bodies; nested `:vec`, `:set`, `:map` with\n939\t    cursor-cell keys, sets of cursor-cell pairs including `[X X]`, sets of\n940\t    sets, under keyed bindings and the result; unique elements and keys\n941\t    under decoded equality) over at least 2000 states, plus at least 200\n942\t    frame-bearing states (cursor cells in an act window, a K-frame\n943\t    window, environments matched to the free environment, and a parked\n944\t    state at a park site) and at least 100 states with install children:\n945\t    every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its root, and\n946\t    renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and census\n947\t    gives an equal root id; refusals are counted and reported (0 under\n948\t    D6); the largest `:work` and `:search` charged are reported.\n949\t19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a task whose census declares a\n950\t    cursor cell the traversal does not reach raises the totality defect\n951\t    (not a refusal) before any row is emitted.\n952\t20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n953\t    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n954\t    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`, `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag`\n955\t    and `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged; the\n956\t    rewritten tests of §8 pass.\n957\t21. `rows-test/work-is-charged-per-byte`: a state whose cursor-cell\n958\t    bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the default\n959\t    budget with the same `:work` as under a 128-character descriptor\n960\t    (rank spelling), and `{:work 1}` refuses `:yin.k/unsupported\n961\t    :resource-limit [:work]` at `emit` and, for a valid carrier, at\n962\t    `decode`.\n963\t22. Budgets and docs: `:label-bytes` is gone (and `:search` in the D5\n964\t    variant); A1–A9 applied in the variant chosen; kondo clean;\n965\t    `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log shows\n966\t    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n967\t\n968\t## 10. Owner questions\n969\t\n970\t1. **D6 or the D5 variant?** Recommended: D6 (a search confined to one\n971\t   conflicting component, measured at 2–13 trials, 6a's roots on the\n972\t   2-cycle and 3-cycle, no structural refusal class to document). The D5\n973\t   variant is the same slice without about 25 lines, with the\n974\t   `:unresolved-cursor-cells` kind and the F4 regression (2-cycles and\n975\t   3-cycles refused) as a documented limitation that D6 can lift later\n976\t   without moving any D1–D4 id.\n977\t2. If the D5 variant: the refusal kind `:unresolved-cursor-cells` as\n978\t   proposed, or the orchestrator's `:resource-limit` (recommended\n979\t   against: it is not a budget, and carrier §10.10 says a resource\n980\t   refusal never stands in for a canonicality verdict)?\n981\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c7b287b-b5f3-49ed-8e51-732a8bb9b9de","uuid":"6d55e556-4ef3-4048-9ce6-f5b6a4b565ee","timestamp":"2026-10-12T08:47:49.078Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-numbering/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.cursor-cell-numbering.md","content":"**rows.cljc, deleted.**\n- `check-label-bytes!` (`:212-230`): the label-size bound; nothing grows\n  any more.\n- Inside `canonical-numbering` (`:236-355`): the label seeding\n  (`:252-255`), `ce-slot`/`ce` (`:257-284`), `positions` (`:285-325`),\n  `classes` (`:326-330`), `refine` (`:331-337`), `search` (`:338-354`),\n  and the `checked-encode`/`checked-key`/`checked-sort` wrappers\n  (`:245-251`). The `[:child (checked-encode id)]` spelling (`:273-275