` with `L = cc-1`\n  (and the renamed task equal); under the D5 variant it asserts the\n  `:unresolved-cursor-cells` refusal with path `[15]` and cells `[A B]`.\n- `intermediate-label-bytes-are-bounded` (`:400-403`) →\n  `seven-cursor-cells-number-by-residue-search` (D6: root `d76d787a…`,\n  11 trials, `{:search 10}` → `:resource-limit [:search]`) or, in the D5\n  variant, `seven-cursor-cells-are-refused` (`:unresolved-cursor-cells`,\n  cells `[a b c d e f g]`).\n- `input-row-bodies-do-not-spend-label-bytes` (`:406-421`) →\n  `large-literals-do-not-spend-work-beyond-their-bytes`, same body: a\n  400000-element literal still emits and decodes under the default\n  budget.\n\n## 9. Acceptance for the rewritten 6a numbering\n\n12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y`,\n    the review counterexample, `[x x y]`, `[x y y]`, `[#{X Y} X]`, the\n    witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]` and the two frame fixtures of §6,\n    `canonical-numbering` returns exactly the maps of §6.\n13. `rows-test/review-counterexample-resolves-by-fixpoint`: `'a #{X Y}`,\n    `'b X` numbers `X cc-1, Y cc-2`; the task renamed and with the set\n    reversed gives the same root; the root is pinned `a3713a5e…`.\n14. `rows-test/component-rule`: `#{X Y}`, `#{[X X] [Y Y]}`, `{X 1, Y 1}`,\n    `#{#{X Y} #{Z W}}` and `[#{X Y} #{X Y}]` number without refusal;\n    element reversal and renaming give equal roots; pins `07eda35d…`,\n    `da69c679…`, `49d4478c…`, `18b70de6…`, `92747c0f…`.\n15. `rows-test/alias-pattern-is-part-of-the-key`: `#{[X X] [Y Z]}` and\n    `{X X, Y Z}` give one root for both enumerations and after renaming,\n    pinned `65ba4530…` and `409548a7…`; `#{[#{X Y} #{X Y}] [#{P Q} #{R S}]}`\n    numbers and is pinned `b35b8e12…`; the witness `[#{#{[A B] [B A]}} A]`\n    numbers `A cc-1, B cc-2`, is pinned `9600fe01…` and decodes.\n16. D6: `rows-test/residue-search`: the 2-cycle, the 3-cycle, the path,\n    the loop plus 2-cycle and the seven-cell state number with the pins\n    of §6 (`0fe898cc…`, `0b181cd4…`, `726a9fbb…`, `858a891e…`,\n    `d76d787a…`), renaming plus shuffling gives equal roots, every\n    carrier decodes, and the 3-cycle under `{:search 1}` refuses\n    `:yin.k/unsupported :resource-limit [:search]`.\n    D5 variant instead: `rows-test/unresolved-cursor-cells-refuse`: the\n    same five states refuse at `emit` with `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind\n    `:unresolved-cursor-cells`, path `[15]` and the component's sorted\n    cursor cells; a carrier of each built with `emit-numbered` decodes to\n    `:yin.k/undecodable :unresolved-cursor-cells` with the path prefixed\n    by the root, never `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`; a parent whose\n    install `'a` holds the 2-cycle refuses at `emit` with path\n    `[12 a 15]` and its `emit-numbered` carrier decodes to the\n    `:yin.k/undecodable` kind with path `[<root> 12 a 15]`.\n17. `rows-test/canonical-roots-are-pinned`: `fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`\n    unchanged; `a3713a5e…`, `4993b5b1…`, `536c810b…`, `7dc3d5c4…`,\n    `6ea03f9b…`, `9600fe01…` added; `55ff168e…` removed.\n18. `rows-test/counterexample-search`: a seeded generator (one to six\n    cursor cells over two bodies; nested `:vec`, `:set`, `:map` with\n    cursor-cell keys, sets of cursor-cell pairs including `[X X]`, sets of\n    sets, under keyed bindings and the result; unique elements and keys\n    under decoded equality) over at least 2000 states, plus at least 200\n    frame-bearing states (cursor cells in an act window, a K-frame\n    window, environments matched to the free environment, and a parked\n    state at a park site) and at least 100 states with install children:\n    every numbered state's carrier decodes and re-emits to its root, and\n    renaming every cursor cell plus shuffling every set, map and census\n    gives an equal root id; refusals are counted and reported (0 under\n    D6); the largest `:work` and `:search` charged are reported.\n19. `rows-test/numbering-is-total`: a task whose census declares a\n    cursor cell the traversal does not reach raises the totality defect\n    (not a refusal) before any row is emitted.\n20. `numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `alias-topology-and-census`,\n    `canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant`,\n    `unordered-containers-are-order-free`, `child-scope-and-shared-child-dag`\n    and `census-is-numeric-from-ten-cursor-cells` pass unchanged; the\n    rewritten tests of §8 pass.\n21. `rows-test/work-is-charged-per-byte`: a state whose cursor-cell\n    bodies carry a 65536-character descriptor numbers under the default\n    budget with the same `:work` as under a 128-character descriptor\n    (rank spelling), and `{:work 1}` refuses `:yin.k/unsupported\n    :resource-limit [:work]` at `emit` and, for a valid carrier, at\n    `decode`.\n22. Budgets and docs: `:label-bytes` is gone (and `:search` in the D5\n    variant); A1–A9 applied in the variant chosen; kondo clean;\n    `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts; Node log shows\n    `Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test`.\n\n## 10. Owner questions\n\n1. **D6 or the D5 variant?** Recommended: D6 (a search confined to one\n   conflicting component, measured at 2–13 trials, 6a's roots on the\n   2-cycle and 3-cycle, no structural refusal class to document). The D5\n   variant is the same slice without about 25 lines, with the\n   `:unresolved-cursor-cells` kind and the F4 regression (2-cycles and\n   3-cycles refused) as a documented limitation that D6 can lift later\n   without moving any D1–D4 id.\n2. If the D5 variant: the refusal kind `:unresolved-cursor-cells` as\n   proposed, or the orchestrator's `:resource-limit` (recommended\n   against: it is not a budget, and carrier §10.10 says a resource\n   refusal never stands in for a canonicality verdict)?\n","numLines":168,"startLine":814,"totalLines":981}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EkuffU3HEXHJWdXAnN4CiZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
